<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=global-positioning-system">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Transport and navigation</p><h1 class="enc-title">Global Positioning System</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as GPS, Navstar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Global Positioning System (GPS) is a satellite-based navigation system owned by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Space Force that gives location and time information anywhere on or near the Earth. The United States <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Department</a> of Defense started the project in 1973, launched the first prototype satellite in 1978 and had 24 satellites operating by 1993. It drew on earlier satellite systems, among them TRANSIT, first tested in 1960, and the Timation satellites, first launched in 1967. After Korean Air Lines Flight 007 was shot down, President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ronald-reagan">Ronald Reagan</a> made the system available for civilian use from 1988.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/global-positioning-system.jpg" alt="Global Positioning System" width="330" height="330" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U.S. Air Force · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GPS_Block_IIIA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1978</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>United States</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Bradford Parkinson · <a href="/empire/united-states">United States</a></dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>TRANSIT, first tested in 1960, was an earlier satellite navigation system that gave a fix about once an hour. The project began in 1973 and the full constellation was operational in 1993.</p><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/radio">Radio<span>1895</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/sputnik-1">Sputnik 1<span>1957</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=global-positioning-system">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
